# Snyk policy for the Edge-1 backend (Snyk project hivemq-edge:build.gradle.kts).
#
# snyk monitor and snyk test read this file from the directory of the build
# file they scan (the path argument hivemq-edge/hivemq-edge in snyk-push.yml
# and snyk-release.yml; the -d before it is the debug flag), so every build
# project and every release project gets these ignores with its snapshot.
# An ignore set only in the Snyk web UI stays on the one project it was set on.
#
# Each entry ignores a finding that no upgrade fixes and that Edge cannot reach.
# The analysis lives in the Linear issue named above the entry; the reason
# below is the one recorded in Snyk.
#
# Fields of each entry:
# - reasonType: the Snyk ignore type (not-vulnerable, wont-fix or
#   temporary-ignore).
# - disregardIfFixable: true, so the finding shows again as soon as Snyk sees
#   an upgrade that fixes it, and the dependency gets updated.
# - ignoredBy: whoever most recently vouched for the entry. Whoever checks an
#   entry again updates it; git history keeps the earlier names.
# - expires: three months after the entry was last vouched for. InfoSec asks
#   for an expiry on every ignore, because auditors read ignores as risk
#   acceptances. When it passes, the finding shows again and Snyk Notifier
#   reopens its Linear issue; whoever checks the entry again sets a new expires
#   along with ignoredBy.
# - created: when the ignore first came into being; it does not change.
#
# Migrated from the Snyk web UI ignores on hivemq-edge:build.gradle.kts [master]
# on 2026-11-21 (EDG-1367).
version: v1.25.0
ignore:
  # EDG-1286 / EDG-1114: jaxb-core XXE (CVE-2026-92877), no upstream fix.
  SNYK-JAVA-ORGGLASSFISHJAXB-20883142:
    - '*':
        reason: >-
          Not reachable in HiveMQ Edge (Edge-1, hivemq-edge) on master from
          352e01605. JAXB unmarshals only operator-controlled local files
          (config.xml, topic-filters.xml, hivemq-extension.xml) and, in the
          MTConnect adapter, agent responses, which are parsed only through an
          XMLInputFactory with DTD support and external entities disabled (both
          for the schemaLocation read and for the JAXB unmarshal), so no
          external entity is resolved. No REST endpoint accepts XML. Milo's
          legacy XML type-dictionary reader (LegacyDataTypeManagerInitializer)
          is not enabled. Checked 352e01605, 2026-11-19, Martin Schönert.
        reasonType: not-vulnerable
        disregardIfFixable: true
        ignoredBy:
          name: Martin Schönert
          email: martin.schoenert@hivemq.com
        expires: 2027-02-25T00:00:00.000Z
        created: 2026-11-19T14:44:00.212Z
  # EDG-1282: jakarta.validation-api 3.1.0, no CVE.
  SNYK-JAVA-JAKARTAVALIDATION-20936881:
    - '*':
        reason: >-
          Not vulnerable: the flaw needs a Java Security Manager, which JDK 24+
          no longer supports (JEP 486). Edge-1 targets Java 25 and runs only on
          JDK 25+. Jakarta Validation is a transitive dependency of
          jersey-server, and Edge doesn't call it.
        reasonType: not-vulnerable
        disregardIfFixable: true
        ignoredBy:
          name: Martin Schönert
          email: martin.schoenert@hivemq.com
        expires: 2027-02-25T00:00:00.000Z
        created: 2026-11-19T18:25:23.281Z
patch: {}
